  "runner_up_case": "The runner-up verdict is MIXED, and its strongest honest case rests on the only truthful fragments in the record: under the 12 August 2025 plea agreement, federal prosecutors dropped seven of the nine counts (WSJ), no jury ever returned a guilty verdict at trial on the criminal charges, and the disposition came by plea with sentencing still pending into late 2025. If 'acquitted' were loosely (and wrongly) read as 'resolved without a trial conviction on every count,' one could argue the claim is partly accurate or accurate only with a heavy qualification. This case fails on the law and the facts: Kwon Do-hyung (권도형), co-founder of Terraform Labs, expressly pleaded guilty in SDNY before Judge Engelmayer on 12 August 2025 to two fraud counts — conspiracy to commit commodities, securities and wire fraud, and wire fraud — which is an admission of guilt and a conviction upon acceptance, the legal opposite of acquittal; he also agreed to forfeit over $19 million; and a jury had already found him and Terraform liable for securities fraud in the SEC civil case in April 2024. No honest reading makes 'acquitted of all US fraud charges in 2025' accurate, so FALSE remains the leading verdict.",
